# CSS/SCSS Architecture (src/css)

## Folder model

- `src/css/foundation/`: global tokens + base styles
  - `_tokens.scss`: CSS variables (colors, glow, fonts)
  - `_base.scss`: body defaults + generic utilities
- `src/css/overrides/`: vendor/framework overrides (ZaUI/ZMP-UI)
  - `_zmp-ui.scss`
- `src/css/features/`: feature/page-level styles (scoped by a root class)
  - `home.scss` -> `.home-page { ... }`
  - `combat.scss` -> `.combat-page { ... }`
  - `lobby.scss` -> `.lobby-page { ... }`
  - `waiting-room.scss` -> `.waiting-page { ... }`

## Import rules

- Global entrypoint stays in `src/css/app.scss` and should only aggregate `foundation/*` + `overrides/*`.
- Feature pages import exactly one file from `src/css/features/<feature>.scss`.
- Avoid importing global styles inside feature files (keep globals in `app.scss`).

## Naming rules

- Feature stylesheet name matches page root class:
  - `home.scss` -> `.home-page`
  - `waiting-room.scss` -> `.waiting-page`
- Keep selectors nested under the page root class to avoid leaking styles globally.

## Reuse guidance

- Prefer CSS variables from `foundation/_tokens.scss` for theme colors/glow.
- If a pattern is reused across 2+ features, extract it into a shared file (e.g. `src/css/components/`) and include it intentionally.

